      "## Definition\n\nPNALD (PN-associated liver disease) = cholestasis + hepatic dysfunction у TPN-dependent infants. Direct bilirubin > 17 µмоль/л (1 мг/дл) > 2 weeks TPN.\n\n## Risk factors\n\n- **Prolonged TPN** > 14 d\n- **Sepsis** (especially CoNS catheter-related)\n- **NEC / SBS** (intestinal injury)\n- **Prematurity** (immature liver)\n- **ELBW** < 1000 g\n- **Lack of enteral nutrition** (gut atrophy)\n- **Pure soy lipid emulsions** (intralipid — pro-inflammatory, phytosterol load)\n\n## Pathophysiology\n\n- Hepatic injury от:\n  - Phytosterols (soy oil)\n  - Hepatic load TPN amino acids\n  - Sepsis-related cholestasis\n  - Lack of enteric stimulation → gut atrophy → bacterial translocation\n\n## Prevention strategies\n\n### 1. Trophic feeds early\n- 10-20 мл/кг/d minimal enteral от 24-48 ч\n- Stimulates gut + reduces cholestasis\n- Even у very unstable preterm — minimal feeds protective\n\n### 2. Avoid pure soy lipid emulsions\n- **SMOFlipid 20 %** preferred (soybean + medium chain + olive + fish oil)\n  - Lapillonne JPGN 2018 — ↓ PNALD risk\n- **Pure intralipid (soy)** — historical, pro-inflammatory\n- **Cyclic lipid administration** — break 8-12 ч/d\n\n### 3. Sepsis prevention bundles\n- **Hand hygiene** strict\n- **Maximal sterile barrier** при line insertion\n- **Chlorhexidine 2 %** skin antiseptic\n- **Daily review necessity** — remove ASAP\n- **CRBSI rates** target < 1 / 1000 catheter days\n\n### 4. Adequate nutrition\n- Avoid excessive amino acid load (4 г/кг/d max)\n- Glucose tolerance — limit hyperglycemia\n- Trace elements: avoid excess copper при cholestasis\n\n### 5. Phenobarbital prophylaxis\n- 5 мг/кг/d × 5 d pre-TPN start (pre-cholestasis prophylaxis controversial)\n- Choleretic effect — limited evidence\n\n## Treatment established PNALD\n\n### 1. Maximize enteral nutrition\n- Advance feeds aggressively if tolerated\n- Wean TPN to minimum needed\n\n### 2. Ursodeoxycholic acid (UDCA)\n- **10-15 мг/кг q12h PO**\n- Choleretic — improves bile flow\n- Bridge while reducing TPN\n\n### 3. Switch lipid emulsion\n- If still on soy → switch к **SMOFlipid**\n- Severe refractory PNALD → **fish oil rescue (Omegaven)** 1 г/кг/d\n  - Composed primarily ω-3 fatty acids\n  - Reverses cholestasis в many cases\n  - Use under specialty consultation (not first-line — limited fatty acid spectrum)\n\n### 4. Address infections\n- Treat any active infection aggressively\n- Recurrent sepsis worsens PNALD significantly\n\n### 5. Cycling TPN\n- 8-12 ч infusion + 12-16 ч off (when stable)\n- Allows hepatic recovery\n\n### 6. Avoid hepatotoxic drugs\n- Acetaminophen — limited course only\n- TMP-SMX — caution\n- Antifungals — monitor\n\n### 7. Severe / refractory\n- **Liver transplant evaluation**\n- **Multivisceral transplant** для combined SBS + liver failure\n- **Specialized centers** (Boston Children's, Pittsburgh, etc.)\n\n## Outcomes\n\n### С modern prevention (SMOFlipid, trophic feeds, bundles)\n- PNALD incidence ↓ 50-70 % vs era pure soy lipids\n- Severe PNALD requiring transplant rare\n\n### Severe PNALD\n- Liver transplant survival ~80 % first year\n- Lifelong immunosuppression after transplant\n\n## Calculator Bordik\n- neo-tpn (PN macronutrient calculator)\n- neo-cholestasis-criteria\n- neo-bili-2022\n- neo-ursodeoxycholic-dose\n\n## Источники\n- Lapillonne A et al. JPGN 2018;67:419 — SMOFlipid\n- Calkins KL et al. JPEN 2014;38:80 — Omegaven rescue\n- ESPGHAN PN 2018\n- Cole CR et al. Pediatrics 2008;122:e573",
