      "neuro",
      "## Recognition\n\n### Clinical types (Volpe classification)\n\n| Тип | Description | EEG correlation |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Subtle** | Eye movements, lip smacking, swimming/cycling, apnea | Variable |\n| **Clonic** | Rhythmic jerking (focal или multifocal) | Strong |\n| **Tonic** | Sustained posturing | Variable |\n| **Myoclonic** | Quick lightning-like jerks | Variable |\n\n### Clinical confounders (mimic seizures)\n- **Jitteriness** — stops with restraint\n- **Benign sleep myoclonus** — only during sleep, normal EEG\n- **Hyperekplexia** — exaggerated startle\n\n## Etiology (in order frequency)\n\n### 1. HIE (most common — 40-60 %)\n- Hypoxic-ischemic encephalopathy\n- Onset usually 12-24 h life\n- Often subtle / clonic\n\n### 2. Stroke (10-20 %)\n- Arterial ischemic stroke (MCA territory most common)\n- Focal seizures predominant\n- Onset 24-72 h\n\n### 3. IVH (5-10 % preterm)\n- Severe IVH grade III-IV\n- Onset variable\n\n### 4. Infection (5-10 %)\n- Meningitis (GBS, E. coli, Listeria)\n- Encephalitis (HSV, CMV)\n- Sepsis\n\n### 5. Metabolic (10 %)\n- Hypoglycemia\n- Hypocalcemia\n- Hypomagnesemia\n- Hyponatremia / hypernatremia\n- Pyridoxine-dependent epilepsy\n- IEM (UCD, organic acidemias, MSUD)\n\n### 6. CNS malformations (rare)\n\n### 7. Drug withdrawal (NAS — usually not seizures, jitteriness)\n\n### 8. Genetic / KCNQ2 epilepsy\n\n## Workup (parallel к treatment)\n\n### Immediate\n- **Glucose** + electrolytes (Ca, Mg)\n- **Blood gas, lactate, ammonia**\n- **CBC, CRP, blood culture**\n- **LP** (если stable patient — CSF cell count, glucose, protein, ПЦР HSV)\n- **Cranial ultrasound**\n\n### Subsequent\n- **EEG / aEEG** continuous (subclinical seizure detection)\n- **MRI brain** (within 5-7 days если HIE; sooner if focal)\n- **TMS / plasma AA / urine OA** (IEM workup)\n- **Pyridoxine 100 мг IV** trial (если refractory — pyridoxine-dependent epilepsy rare but treatable)\n- **Genetic testing** (если familial, refractory, no other cause)\n\n## Pharmacological algorithm (NeoLEV2 + Cochrane)\n\n### First-line: Phenobarbital\n- **Loading: 20 мг/кг IV slow over 15-20 мин**\n- Если seizures persist: repeat 10 мг/кг q15-30 мин до cumulative 40 мг/кг\n- Maintenance: 3-5 мг/кг q24h IV/PO (start 24 ч после loading)\n- Therapeutic level 20-40 мг/л\n\n### Second-line: Levetiracetam (NeoLEV2 — equivalent efficacy)\n- **Loading: 40-60 мг/кг IV (max 100 мг/кг)**\n- Maintenance: 20-40 мг/кг q12h IV/PO\n- **Better safety profile vs phenobarbital** (less sedation, no cognitive concerns)\n- **Many centers now use as FIRST-line**\n\n### Third-line: Phenytoin или Fosphenytoin\n- **Phenytoin loading: 15-20 мг/кг IV slow over 20-30 мин**\n- Fosphenytoin: 15-20 мг/кг PE IV (faster — over 5-10 мин)\n- Maintenance: 3-5 мг/кг q24h\n- Cardiac monitoring critical (arrhythmias, hypotension)\n\n### Refractory: Midazolam infusion или Lidocaine\n- **Midazolam:** bolus 0.05-0.15 мг/кг IV; infusion 0.06-0.4 мг/кг/h\n- **Lidocaine:** loading 2 мг/кг IV; infusion 6 мг/кг/h × 4 h, then 4 мг/кг/h × 12 h, then 2 мг/кг/h × 12 h\n- ⚠️ Lidocaine — НЕ при concurrent phenytoin (additive cardiac toxicity)\n\n### Pyridoxine (B6) trial\n- При refractory seizures (esp. neonatal-onset epilepsy): **100 мг IV trial**\n- Pyridoxine-dependent epilepsy — rare, но treatable\n\n## Cooling для HIE\nЕсли seizures + perinatal hypoxic event — cooling protocol активируется параллельно (см. art-cooling).\n\n## Calculator Bordik\n- neo-asphyxia-criteria, neo-hie-cooling\n- thompson (Thompson/Sarnat staging)\n- neo-phenobarbital-dose\n- neo-levetiracetam-dose\n- neo-midazolam-dose\n- neo-pyridoxine-dose\n\n## Источники\n- Sharpe C et al. Pediatrics 2020;145:e20193182 — NeoLEV2\n- Glass HC et al. J Pediatr 2017;184:200\n- Painter MJ et al. NEJM 1999;341:485\n- ILAE Neonatal Seizures Classification 2021\n- КР МЗ РФ \"Неонатальные судороги\" 2024",
